[agent] ## What was delivered
[agent] Feature group **`accountsd00439`, version 1** in project `mlpab3010fa`'s feature store, with:
[agent] - primary key `row_id`, event-time column `updated_at` (bigint, epoch milliseconds)
[agent] - `online_enabled: True` — features are in both the offline store and the online store for low-latency lookup
[agent] ## How it got there
[agent] 1. Direct ingestion from the local SDK client failed: the Python engine's delta-rs writer dials HopsFS (`10.112.103.124:8020`) over raw TCP, which the local sandbox blocks (only the localhost HTTP proxy is reachable; I had to drop `NO_PROXY` inside the script even for the REST API).
[agent] 2. So the work was moved fully onto the platform: the three batch CSVs were uploaded to `Resources/accounts_batches/` via the dataset REST API, and a PySpark job (`accountsd00439_ingest`) was created and run on the cluster. The job reads the batches, keeps the latest revision per `row_id` (window over `updated_at` descending), and inserts into the feature group.
